WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.332
[MUSIC]

00:00:07.332 --> 00:00:10.472
SPEAKER: Some obligations
arise from consent.

00:00:10.489 --> 00:00:17.699
If I hire someone to paint my house,
and he does so, I'm obligated to pay.

00:00:17.704 --> 00:00:22.004
But can obligations also arise
without an act of consent?

00:00:22.004 --> 00:00:26.504
Consider the story about the
18th-century Scottish philosopher David

00:00:26.527 --> 00:00:28.487
Hume.

00:00:28.509 --> 00:00:30.819
Hume owned a house in Edinburgh.

00:00:30.819 --> 00:00:33.699
He rented it to his
friend James Boswell,

00:00:33.718 --> 00:00:37.778
who in turn sublet it to a sub-tenant.

00:00:37.791 --> 00:00:42.061
The sub-tenant decided that
the house needed some repairs.

00:00:42.062 --> 00:00:47.437
He hired a contractor to do the
work without consulting Hume.

00:00:47.437 --> 00:00:51.547
The contractor made the repairs
and sent the bill to Hume.

00:00:51.549 --> 00:00:57.415
Hume refused to pay on the
grounds that he had not consented.

00:00:57.415 --> 00:01:00.315
He hadn't hired the contractor.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:02.380
The case went to court.

00:01:02.389 --> 00:01:06.619
The contractor acknowledged
that Hume had not consented.

00:01:06.619 --> 00:01:09.019
But the house needed the repairs.

00:01:09.022 --> 00:01:11.097
And he had performed them.

00:01:11.097 --> 00:01:17.250
The court ruled in the contractor's
favor and required Hume to pay him.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:20.253
Put aside whatever the law
might have been at the time.

00:01:20.253 --> 00:01:24.393
How would you have decided the
case from a moral point of view?

00:01:24.416 --> 00:01:28.567
Do you think that Hume is morally
obligated to pay this contractor?

00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:32.657
[MUSIC]

